/**

@page page_exahype_faq FAQ and troubleshooting

# The space-time predictor diverged

An ADER-DG solver without a limiter ends the run when the Picard iteration of
a cell diverges, and names the cell centre. A solver with a subcell limiter
marks the cell as troubled and recomputes it with the finite-volume scheme.
Reduce the time step factor or add a limiter.

# The maximum eigenvalue is not finite

An adaptive solver ends the run with a non-critical assertion when a cell
reports an infinite or negative wave speed and writes the last solution. The
plotted snapshot shows the cell; check the initial condition and the
boundary conditions of that cell.

# The solver memory grows in segments

A pool reserves whole segments of slots, so the reported solver memory rises
in steps of one segment per pool when the grid grows and stays when the grid
shrinks until the last segment holds no live slot.

*/
